<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed groups continue ambushing civilians, with killings reported in Jebel Boma County and a road ambush in Warrap County, while the SSPDF killed two Kapoeta youth after an arrest and the Kapoeta South Commissioner confirmed the killing of an SPLM secretary and a friend. A Christian woman was killed for refusing a forced marriage to a Muslim man and two pastors were wounded in a separate attack, prompting women in Greater Mundri to demand protection. The Ministry of Gender and stakeholders reviewed draft guidelines for safe houses for GBV survivors, and South Sudan condemned Iran missile and drone attacks in the Middle East. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Social News XYZ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUEFVX3lxTE1pbkFIUFo0MnJCaWJMejVKbGRkZkRNZ3BVQ296Z21IU0RQZV9HVkFCbk1FRl9lekdwelRjR25ISVdCNVZnM0RwLTZTam5aUmU4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudan Tribune&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;OkayAfrica&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxQbmE0ZDd1cV9UbmdtRVVtNGk3cVJManFwSnFDNEZRSmNoTll4ZW1RcmZKQjhlVDVZQ2lwUGpmUUJwd2dRLUZZZ004VW9NUUt4dmZDcmNhb3RObDNIeFRrQWx6ckNDNjZkODkzaGxTQ1BjakI0N2hNZEFQYVNZRWZDbUdZOHRHbmFpNmNVMzBtZDNrRnlPUjdHbHBReEQxSEpObFFaUG1oTQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Pretoria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPeExHSlFyZkVkaVItZVRMaW1nM2hHSkdvMUNjdV9yRUo0UHBFY01qNTRweGRuRVlEVjJ1bXd3ZWQ2ek05MmZhUjFaaFBoejVTc09XWWstSC1DQl9vRzdJRThFWjh4cTBhaXdMZkxtcl9LR0tqaTBIcDRmSW9JYmUxSXpsNENWbkFDM1IwbjBiWDBNYU9qMUMxNzJrSXpibU1SdjdSbUFVbmZoWEdKenQ1WWRR?oc=5&quot;&gt;Premier Christian News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPbWxPcGZSSS1OMkhoYUt4V2dWaG5semQ2Zlls